# Agent Operating Rules (JlightCalendar-wearOS)

This project strictly adheres to the standards defined in the root [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

Key Directives:
1. Always run `./gradlew check lintDebug` (or `.\gradlew.bat check lintDebug` on Windows) directly before marking any task as complete. Never create wrapper PowerShell or shell scripts around Gradle.
2. Read `specs/active/` and `docs/architecture/overview.md` before implementing features.
3. Review `docs/adr/` before introducing new dependencies in `gradle/libs.versions.toml` or altering architectural patterns.
4. Preserve Clean Architecture boundaries (`ui/`, `tile/`, and `complication/` depend only on `domain/`) and Local Wall-Clock Time parity (`java.time.LocalDate` / `LocalTime`).
5. Follow conventional commit format (`feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`) on feature branches (`feat/*`, `fix/*`, `chore/*`).
6. For PR reviews, follow the evaluation rules in `.agents/pr-reviewer.md` and `.ci-reviewer.yml`.
